(255, 'SQL', 'SELECT d.Name AS Department, e.Name AS Employee, e.Salary\nFROM Employee e\nJOIN Department d ON e.DepartmentId = d.Id\nWHERE (e.DepartmentId, e.Salary) IN (\n    SELECT DepartmentId, MAX(Salary)\n    FROM Employee\n    GROUP BY DepartmentId\n);', NULL, 1),
(256, 'TEXT', '1. **连接**：TCP面向连接，需三次握手；UDP无连接，直接发送。\n2. **可靠性**：TCP可靠，有确认、重传、排序、去重；UDP不可靠，不保证送达和顺序。\n3. **传输方式**：TCP面向字节流；UDP面向数据报，保留报文边界。\n4. **速度与开销**：TCP头部20字节起，开销大、速度慢；UDP头部仅8字节，开销小、速度快。\n5. **拥塞与流量控制**：TCP有拥塞控制和流量控制；UDP无。\n6. **通信模式**：TCP仅一对一；UDP支持一对一、一对多、多对多（广播、组播）。\n7. **适用场景**：TCP用于文件传输、网页等要求可靠的场景；UDP用于直播、游戏、DNS等重实时低延迟场景。', NULL, 1),
(257, 'TEXT', '1. **安全性**：HTTP明文传输，易被窃听篡改；HTTPS在HTTP下加入TLS/SSL加密，保证机密性、完整性。\n\n2. **端口**：HTTP默认80，HTTPS默认443。\n\n3. **证书**：HTTPS需CA颁发证书验证服务器身份，防中间人攻击；HTTP无身份验证。\n\n4. **性能**：HTTPS因加解密和握手，延迟略高、消耗更多CPU，但现代优化后差距很小。\n\n5. **URL**：HTTPS以https://开头，HTTP为http://。\n\n核心：HTTPS = HTTP + TLS，解决明文传输的安全问题。', NULL, 1),
(258, 'TEXT', 'HTTP 常见请求方法：\n\n- **GET**：获取资源，参数在 URL，幂等、可缓存，不改变服务端状态。\n- **POST**：提交数据、创建资源，参数在请求体，非幂等，不可缓存。\n- **PUT**：全量更新资源，幂等，客户端提供完整资源。\n- **PATCH**：局部更新资源，非幂等。\n- **DELETE**：删除资源，幂等。\n- **HEAD**：同 GET 但只返回响应头，用于探测。\n- **OPTIONS**：查询支持的方法，用于 CORS 预检。\n\n核心区分：**幂等性**（GET/PUT/DELETE 幂等，POST 非幂等）与**安全性**（GET/HEAD 安全，不修改资源）。', NULL, 1),
(259, 'TEXT', '**核心区别：**\n\n1. **存储位置**：Cookie 存在客户端浏览器；Session 存在服务端（Session ID 通常借 Cookie 传给客户端）。\n2. **安全性**：Cookie 明文可见、可篡改，安全性低；Session 存服务端，相对安全。\n3. **容量**：Cookie 单个约 4KB 且数量受限；Session 受服务器内存限制，容量更大。\n4. **性能**：Cookie 随每次请求发送，增加带宽；Session 存服务端，但高并发下占内存、需考虑共享。\n5. **生命周期**：Cookie 可设过期时间长期保存；Session 随会话结束或超时失效。\n\n**使用场景**：Cookie 用于记住登录状态、偏好设置等非敏感轻量数据；Session 用于存用户身份、权限等敏感信息。', NULL, 1),
(260, 'TEXT', '**跨域问题**：浏览器同源策略限制，协议、域名、端口任一不同即为跨域，导致 AJAX 请求被拦截（请求可能发出，但响应被阻止）。\n\n**常见解决方法**：\n1. **CORS**：服务端设置 `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` 等响应头，最主流。\n2. **Nginx 反向代理**：同源访问代理服务器，由服务器转发，规避浏览器限制。\n3. **JSONP**：利用 script 标签，仅支持 GET，已少用。\n4. **开发环境代理**：如 webpack/vite devServer proxy。\n5. **postMessage / document.domain**：用于窗口间通信或子域场景。\n\n**核心**：跨域是浏览器行为，服务端之间无跨域；CORS 需处理预检请求（OPTIONS）。', NULL, 1),
(261, 'TEXT', '1. **定义**：进程是资源分配的基本单位；线程是CPU调度的基本单位。\n2. **资源**：进程有独立地址空间和资源；线程共享所属进程的资源（内存、文件等），仅独享栈和寄存器。\n3. **开销**：进程创建、切换、销毁开销大；线程轻量，切换开销小。\n4. **通信**：进程间通信需借助IPC（管道、共享内存等）；线程可直接读写共享内存，但需同步。\n5. **独立性**：进程相互隔离，一个崩溃不影响其他；线程共享进程，一个线程崩溃可能导致整个进程退出。\n6. **关系**：一个进程可含多个线程，线程依附于进程存在。', NULL, 1),
(262, 'TEXT', '死锁产生的四个必要条件：\n\n1. **互斥**：资源一次只能被一个进程占用。\n2. **占有并等待**：进程已持有至少一个资源，同时又在等待其他被占用的资源。\n3. **不可剥夺**：资源只能由持有它的进程主动释放，不能被强行抢占。\n4. **循环等待**：存在一个进程与资源的环形等待链，每个进程都在等待下一个进程持有的资源。\n\n四个条件同时满足才可能死锁，破坏其中任一条件即可预防死锁。', NULL, 1),
(263, 'TEXT', '常见进程调度算法：\n\n- **FCFS（先来先服务）**：按到达顺序执行，非抢占。实现简单，但长作业先到会导致短作业等待，平均等待时间长（护航效应）。\n- **SJF（短作业优先）**：选运行时间最短的进程，分抢占/非抢占。平均等待时间最优，但需预知运行时间，长作业可能饥饿。\n- **RR（时间片轮转）**：按到达顺序轮流执行固定时间片，抢占式。响应快、公平，适合分时系统；时间片过大退化为FCFS，过小则切换开销大。\n- **优先级调度**：按优先级选进程，分抢占/非抢占，低优先级可能饥饿，可用老化解决。\n- **多级反馈队列**：多队列不同优先级+时间片，兼顾响应与吞吐，综合性强。', NULL, 1),
(264, 'TEXT', '常见页面置换算法：\n\n- **OPT（最佳置换）**：淘汰未来最长时间不被访问的页面。缺页率最低，但需预知未来，仅作理论基准。\n- **FIFO（先进先出）**：淘汰最早进入内存的页面。实现简单，但可能淘汰常用页，且存在 Belady 异常（增加物理块反而缺页增多）。\n- **LRU（最近最久未使用）**：淘汰最长时间未被访问的页面。基于局部性原理，性能接近 OPT，但需记录访问历史，开销较大。\n- **Clock（时钟）**：LRU 的近似，用循环队列加访问位，访问位置 1，淘汰时扫描置 0，兼顾性能与开销。\n\n考点：各算法淘汰依据、优缺点、Belady 异常及 LRU 与 OPT 的区别。', NULL, 1),
(265, 'TEXT', '银行家算法是操作系统的**死锁避免**算法。\n\n- **原理**：进程运行前先声明最大资源需求。系统分配资源前，先试探性分配，再执行**安全性检查**：判断是否存在一个安全序列，使所有进程能依次获得所需资源并完成。若存在则真正分配，否则拒绝，让进程等待。\n- **核心数据结构**：可利用资源、最大需求、已分配、需求矩阵。\n- **作用**：在资源分配前预判是否会导致系统进入不安全状态，从而**避免死锁**，而非事后检测或解除。\n- **局限**：需预知最大需求、进程数固定、资源单一时效率低，实际中较少直接使用。', NULL, 1),
(266, 'TEXT', '**概念**：保证一个类仅有一个实例，并提供全局访问点。\n\n**实现要点**：\n1. 私有构造器，禁止外部 new。\n2. 静态私有实例变量。\n3. 提供静态公有获取方法。\n\n**常见方式**：\n- 饿汉式：类加载即创建，线程安全但可能浪费。\n- 懒汉式：延迟创建，需加锁或用双重检查锁保证线程安全。\n- 静态内部类：延迟加载且线程安全，推荐。\n- 枚举：最简洁，天然防反射和反序列化破坏。\n\n**使用场景**：全局配置、连接池、线程池、日志对象、缓存等需唯一实例且频繁访问的资源。', NULL, 1),
(267, 'TEXT', '工厂模式是创建型设计模式，用工厂封装对象创建过程，使调用方与具体类解耦。\n\n分类：\n1. 简单工厂：一个工厂类按参数创建不同产品，不属于GOF23，违反开闭原则。\n2. 工厂方法：定义创建接口，由子类决定实例化哪个类，符合开闭原则。\n3. 抽象工厂：创建一系列相关产品族，适合多产品线组合。\n\n使用场景：对象创建逻辑复杂或需隐藏具体实现；产品类型可能扩展；需统一管理一族产品。', NULL, 1),
(268, 'TEXT', '**概念**：观察者模式定义一对多依赖关系，当被观察者（Subject）状态改变时，自动通知所有观察者（Observer）更新。\n\n**核心角色**：\n- Subject：维护观察者列表，提供注册/注销/通知接口。\n- Observer：定义更新接口，接收通知。\n\n**使用场景**：\n- 事件驱动系统：GUI 事件监听、按钮点击回调。\n- 消息订阅：发布-订阅、MQ、Redis 订阅。\n- 数据联动：MVC 中 Model 变化通知 View 刷新。\n- 跨模块解耦：状态变更需通知多个不相关模块。\n\n**优点**：解耦、支持广播、符合开闭原则。\n**缺点**：通知顺序不可控、观察者过多影响性能、可能循环依赖。', NULL, 1),
(269, 'TEXT', '**概念**：策略模式定义一系列算法，将每个算法封装成独立类并可相互替换，使算法的变化独立于使用它的客户端。\n\n**核心角色**：抽象策略（接口）、具体策略（实现类）、上下文（持有策略并调用）。\n\n**使用场景**：\n1. 同一问题有多种算法，需运行时动态切换（如排序、支付方式、促销计算）。\n2. 用多分支 if-else/switch 判断不同行为，且分支会持续扩展。\n3. 需要隔离算法实现细节，避免客户端依赖具体算法。\n\n**优点**：符合开闭原则，消除条件分支，算法可复用、易扩展。\n**缺点**：策略类增多，客户端需了解各策略差异。', NULL, 1),
(270, 'TEXT', 'MVC是一种分层架构模式，将应用分为三层：\n\n- **Model（模型）**：封装数据和业务逻辑，负责数据的存取与状态管理，不依赖View和Controller。\n- **View（视图）**：负责数据展示和用户界面渲染，只呈现Model的数据，不处理业务逻辑。\n- **Controller（控制器）**：接收用户输入，调用Model处理业务，再选择合适的View返回结果，起协调调度作用。\n\n核心思想是**关注点分离**：三者职责单一、解耦，便于维护、复用和测试。', NULL, 1),
(271, 'TEXT', '面向对象三大特性：\n\n1. **封装**：将数据和操作数据的方法绑定在一起，隐藏内部实现细节，仅对外暴露必要接口。目的是降低耦合、提高安全性和可维护性。\n\n2. **继承**：子类复用父类的属性和方法，并可扩展或重写。目的是代码复用、建立类之间的层次关系。分为单继承和多继承。\n\n3. **多态**：同一接口在不同对象上有不同表现。分为编译时多态（重载）和运行时多态（重写，依赖继承与父类引用指向子类对象）。目的是提高扩展性和灵活性。\n\n三者关系：封装是基础，继承是手段，多态是目的。', NULL, 1),
(272, 'TEXT', '1. **定义**：抽象类用 abstract class 声明，可含抽象方法和具体方法；接口用 interface 声明，方法默认 public abstract（Java 8 后可有 default、static 方法）。\n\n2. **继承**：类只能单继承抽象类，但可实现多个接口。\n\n3. **成员变量**：抽象类可有普通变量、常量；接口变量默认 public static final 常量。\n\n4. **构造器**：抽象类有构造器；接口没有。\n\n5. **访问修饰符**：抽象类方法可用各种修饰符；接口方法默认 public。\n\n6. **设计语义**：抽象类表示“is-a”，用于代码复用；接口表示“can-do”，用于定义行为契约、解耦。\n\n7. **使用场景**：共性逻辑用抽象类，扩展能力用接口。', NULL, 1),
(273, 'TEXT', '**重载（Overload）**：同一类中，方法名相同、参数列表不同（个数、类型、顺序），与返回值无关，编译期确定，是编译时多态。\n\n**重写（Override）**：子类重新实现父类方法，方法名、参数列表、返回值（协变除外）必须相同，访问权限不能更严，不能重写 private/static/final 方法，运行期确定，是运行时多态。\n\n**核心区别**：\n1. 范围：重载同类内，重写发生在父子类间。\n2. 签名：重载参数必须不同，重写参数必须相同。\n3. 时机：重载编译期绑定，重写运行期绑定。\n4. 目的：重载扩展同类方法形式，重写改变父类行为。', NULL, 1),
(274, 'TEXT', '1. **指代对象**：this 指向当前对象自身；super 指向当前对象的父类部分（父类实例）。\n2. **访问成员**：this 访问本类成员（属性、方法），可区分同名参数与成员变量；super 访问父类成员，用于调用被子类重写的方法或父类属性。\n3. **调用构造器**：this() 调用本类其他构造器；super() 调用父类构造器。二者都必须放在构造器首行，且不能同时出现。\n4. **使用场景**：this 用于区分变量、链式调用、返回当前对象；super 用于子类访问父类被覆盖的成员、初始化父类。\n5. **本质**：this 是当前对象引用；super 不是引用，只是访问父类成员的语法关键字。', NULL, 1),
(275, 'TEXT', '**概念**：继承是面向对象中让子类复用父类属性和方法的机制，表达“is-a”关系。\n\n**优点**：\n1. 代码复用，减少冗余。\n2. 提高可扩展性，子类可扩展父类功能。\n3. 多态基础，便于统一接口编程。\n\n**缺点**：\n1. 耦合度高，父类改动易影响子类（脆弱基类问题）。\n2. 破坏封装，子类依赖父类实现细节。\n3. 继承层次过深导致结构复杂、难维护。\n4. 灵活性差，运行期难以改变继承关系，常建议优先组合而非继承。', NULL, 1),
(276, 'TEXT', '函数式编程核心概念：\n\n1. **纯函数**：相同输入必得相同输出，无副作用，不修改外部状态。\n2. **不可变性**：数据一旦创建不可更改，变更通过创建新数据实现。\n3. **一等函数**：函数可作为参数传递、作为返回值、赋值给变量。\n4. **高阶函数**：接收函数或返回函数的函数，如 map、filter、reduce。\n5. **函数组合**：将小函数组合成复杂函数，强调声明式而非命令式。\n6. **引用透明**：表达式可被其计算结果替换而不影响程序。\n\n特点：无副作用、易于测试与并发、代码简洁可推理；但可能带来性能开销与学习成本。', NULL, 1),
(277, 'TEXT', 'Lambda表达式是匿名函数，用于简化函数式接口（仅一个抽象方法的接口）的实例化。\n\n核心要点：\n1. 语法：(参数) -> 表达式或代码块，参数类型可省略，由编译器推断。\n2. 本质：编译后生成函数式接口的实现对象，可替代匿名内部类。\n3. 前提：目标类型必须是函数式接口，常用@FunctionalInterface标注。\n4. 变量捕获：只能引用final或事实上的final局部变量。\n5. 典型应用：集合遍历、排序、Stream流操作、线程创建。\n6. 与方法引用（::）配合，进一步简化代码。', NULL, 1),
(278, 'TEXT', 'Stream API用于对集合进行声明式、函数式处理，核心用法：\n\n1. **创建**：集合.stream()、Arrays.stream()、Stream.of()。\n2. **中间操作**（惰性，返回新流）：filter过滤、map映射、flatMap扁平化、distinct去重、sorted排序、limit/skip截取。\n3. **终端操作**（触发执行）：forEach遍历、collect收集、reduce归约、count、anyMatch/allMatch、findFirst。\n4. **特性**：惰性求值，需终端操作才执行；不修改原数据；支持串行与parallelStream并行。\n\n核心思想：链式调用，将数据处理流程化。', NULL, 1),
(279, 'TEXT', '纯函数指满足以下两个条件的函数：\n\n1. **相同输入必返回相同输出**：结果只由入参决定，不依赖外部可变状态、时间、随机数等。\n2. **无副作用**：不修改外部状态，如不改全局变量、不修改入参、不做 I/O、不发请求、不打印日志。\n\n特点与意义：\n\n- **可预测**：调用结果稳定，便于推理和测试。\n- **易测试**：无需 mock 外部环境，给定输入即可断言输出。\n- **可缓存**：相同输入可复用结果（如 memoization）。\n- **利于并发**：不共享可变状态，天然线程安全。\n- **易组合**：可作为构建函数式编程的基础单元。\n\n核心一句话：**输出只依赖输入，且不产生任何可观察的副作用。**', NULL, 1),
(280, 'TEXT', '**概念**：高阶函数是满足以下任一条件的函数：接收一个或多个函数作为参数；或返回一个函数作为结果。本质是把函数当作一等公民，可像普通值一样传递和返回。\n\n**使用场景**：\n1. **回调**：事件处理、异步回调，将行为参数化。\n2. **数组操作**：map、filter、reduce 等，用函数描述处理逻辑。\n3. **函数组合与柯里化**：compose、curry，复用和拼装逻辑。\n4. **装饰/增强**：在不改原函数前提下添加日志、缓存、权限等（如装饰器）。\n5. **抽象控制流**：把循环、条件等通用逻辑封装，只暴露变化部分。\n\n**核心价值**：提升抽象层次、代码复用性与可组合性。', NULL, 1),
(281, 'TEXT', '**作用**：synchronized 用于实现线程同步，保证同一时刻只有一个线程执行临界区代码，具备原子性、可见性、有序性。\n\n**三种用法**：\n1. 修饰实例方法：锁为当前实例对象。\n2. 修饰静态方法：锁为当前类的 Class 对象。\n3. 修饰代码块：锁为括号内指定对象。\n\n**原理**：基于对象监视器（Monitor），通过 monitorenter/monitorexit 指令实现，锁信息存于对象头 Mark Word。\n\n**特性**：可重入、非公平（默认）、JDK1.6 后引入偏向锁、轻量级锁、自旋等优化，性能大幅提升。', NULL, 1),
(282, 'TEXT', '**作用**：保证变量在多线程间的**可见性**和**有序性**，但不保证**原子性**。\n\n**原理**：\n1. **可见性**：写操作后立即刷回主内存，读操作直接从主内存读取，使其他线程能立即看到最新值。\n2. **有序性**：通过内存屏障禁止指令重排序，保证 volatile 读写前后的指令不被乱序执行。\n3. **不保证原子性**：如 `i++` 包含读、改、写三步，多线程下仍会出错，需配合锁或原子类。\n\n**典型场景**：状态标志位、双重检查锁定的单例（防止指令重排）。\n\n**与 synchronized 区别**：volatile 轻量，仅保证可见性和有序性；synchronized 还保证原子性和互斥。', NULL, 1),
(283, 'TEXT', '**概念**：线程池是预先创建并复用线程的并发框架，任务提交到队列，由空闲线程取出执行，避免频繁创建销毁线程。\n\n**优点**：\n1. 降低资源消耗，复用线程；\n2. 提高响应速度，任务到达即执行；\n3. 统一管理，可控并发数，防止资源耗尽；\n4. 提供任务队列、拒绝策略等扩展能力。\n\n**常见实现**：\n- Java：`ThreadPoolExecutor`（核心参数：核心/最大线程数、队列、拒绝策略），及 `Executors` 工具类；\n- 其他：C++ 手写线程池、Go 的 goroutine 调度、Python `concurrent.futures`。\n\n**核心考点**：任务调度流程、参数配置、拒绝策略、线程复用原理。', NULL, 1),
(284, 'TEXT', 'CAS（Compare-And-Swap）是一种无锁原子操作，用于实现并发同步。\n\n**概念**：包含三个操作数——内存位置V、预期旧值A、新值B。仅当V的当前值等于A时，才将V更新为B，否则不做任何操作。整个比较与交换过程由硬件保证原子性。\n\n**原理**：\n1. CPU提供原子指令（如x86的cmpxchg）实现，无需加锁。\n2. 返回操作是否成功，失败通常配合自旋重试。\n3. 存在ABA问题：值从A改为B又改回A，CAS无法察觉，可用版本号（如AtomicStampedReference）解决。\n\n**应用**：Java的AtomicInteger、AQS、无锁队列等底层均基于CAS。', NULL, 1),
(285, 'TEXT', 'AQS（AbstractQueuedSynchronizer）是JUC中构建锁和同步器的核心框架，基于模板方法模式。\n\n核心要点：\n1. **核心结构**：一个volatile的state状态位 + 一个FIFO双向等待队列（CLH变体）。\n2. **state含义**：由子类定义，如ReentrantLock表示重入次数，Semaphore表示许可数。\n3. **获取/释放**：通过CAS修改state，失败则封装成Node入队并阻塞（LockSupport.park）。\n4. **两种模式**：独占（如ReentrantLock）和共享（如Semaphore、CountDownLatch）。\n5. **作用**：屏蔽排队、阻塞、唤醒等复杂细节，子类只需实现tryAcquire/tryRelease等方法即可自定义同步器。', NULL, 1),
(286, 'TEXT', 'CAP定理：分布式系统中，一致性（Consistency）、可用性（Availability）、分区容错性（Partition tolerance）三者不可同时满足，最多满足两个。\n\n- **一致性C**：所有节点同一时刻看到相同数据，读操作总能返回最新写入值。\n- **可用性A**：每个请求都能在有限时间内得到非错误响应，但不保证是最新数据。\n- **分区容错性P**：网络分区（节点间消息丢失或延迟）时系统仍能继续运行。\n\n由于网络分区在分布式系统中不可避免，P通常必须保留，因此实际是在C和A之间取舍：如CP（ZooKeeper）、AP（Cassandra）。', NULL, 1),
(287, 'TEXT', '分布式事务指事务操作跨多个节点/数据源，需保证整体ACID。\n\n常见方案：\n1. **2PC/3PC**：协调者统一提交，强一致但阻塞、性能差。\n2. **TCC**：Try-Confirm-Cancel，业务层补偿，侵入性强。\n3. **本地消息表/事务消息**：借助MQ最终一致，实现简单。\n4. **Saga**：长事务拆分为子事务，失败逐级补偿。\n5. **Seata**：AT模式自动补偿，对业务侵入小。\n\n核心权衡：强一致（2PC）vs 最终一致（消息、Saga、TCC）。', NULL, 1),
(288, 'TEXT', '**概念**：一致性哈希将哈希空间组织成环（0~2³²-1），节点和数据都映射到环上，数据顺时针归属最近的节点。增删节点时只影响相邻区间，而非全部重映射。\n\n**核心机制**：\n- 普通哈希取模，节点数变化会导致几乎所有 key 失效；一致性哈希只迁移约 1/N 的数据。\n- 用**虚拟节点**解决数据倾斜：每个物理节点映射多个虚拟节点，使分布更均匀。\n\n**应用场景**：\n- 分布式缓存（如 Redis 集群）的 key 路由。\n- 负载均衡、分布式存储的数据分片。\n- 需动态扩缩容且要求最小数据迁移的场景。', NULL, 1),
(289, 'TEXT', '**概念**：将请求按策略分发到多台服务器，避免单点过载。\n\n**作用**：\n- 提升吞吐量与可用性\n- 避免单点故障，支持水平扩展\n- 便于维护与灰度发布\n\n**常见算法**：\n- 轮询 / 加权轮询：依次分发，按性能加权\n- 随机 / 加权随机\n- 最少连接：发给当前连接最少的节点\n- 一致性哈希：同key固定落到同节点，减少缓存失效\n- IP哈希：同IP固定节点，保持会话\n\n**层次**：四层（LVS，基于IP/端口）、七层（Nginx，基于URL/Header）。', NULL, 1),
(290, 'TEXT', '**概念**：将单一应用按业务拆分为多个独立部署的小服务，服务间通过轻量级通信（如 HTTP/RPC）协作，每个服务可独立开发、部署、扩展。\n\n**优点**：\n- 服务解耦，边界清晰，便于团队并行开发\n- 独立部署与扩容，故障隔离，单点问题不影响全局\n- 技术栈灵活，可按服务选型\n\n**缺点**：\n- 分布式复杂度高：网络延迟、调用失败、数据一致性难保证\n- 运维成本大：需服务发现、配置中心、链路追踪、监控等配套\n- 调试与测试困难，跨服务事务处理复杂\n\n**核心考点**：拆分粒度、分布式带来的复杂度与治理成本，适用场景是业务复杂、团队规模大的系统。', NULL, 1),
(291, 'TEXT', '学习编程的核心方法：\n\n1. **选对语言与方向**：根据目标（后端、前端、数据）选一门主流语言，避免频繁切换。\n2. **系统学习基础**：掌握语法、数据结构、算法、操作系统、网络等核心知识。\n3. **动手实践**：通过写小项目、刷题、复现轮子加深理解，拒绝只看不写。\n4. **阅读源码与文档**：学习优秀开源项目，理解工程化写法与设计思想。\n5. **调试与总结**：善用调试工具，记录踩坑与解决方案，形成知识体系。\n6. **持续迭代**：参与真实项目或开源，接受代码评审，保持输入与输出平衡。\n\n关键：**刻意练习 + 项目驱动 + 持续反馈**。', NULL, 1),
(292, 'TEXT', '**核心考点：稳定性、上进心、岗位匹配度。**\n\n回答分三层：\n\n1. **短期（1年）**：快速熟悉业务与团队协作，独立承担岗位职责，达到考核要求。\n2. **中期（2-3年）**：深耕专业领域，提升核心技能，能主导项目或模块，成为团队骨干。\n3. **长期（3-5年）**：结合公司发展，向更高阶方向（技术专家或管理）成长，持续为团队创造价值。\n\n**要点**：规划须与应聘岗位、公司方向一致；体现踏实、稳定、有目标，避免空泛或显得随时跳槽。', NULL, 1),
(293, 'TEXT', '核心考点：用 STAR 法则讲清项目，突出个人贡献与量化结果。\n\n- **背景**：一句话说明项目目标、规模、你的角色。\n- **挑战**：点明最难的技术或协作难点（如高并发、性能瓶颈、跨团队）。\n- **行动**：重点讲“我”做了什么，而非团队做了什么；说清技术选型与决策理由。\n- **结果**：用数据量化，如性能提升、成本下降、上线收益。\n- **反思**：一句总结收获或改进点。\n\n避免流水账，突出个人不可替代性，准备被追问细节。', NULL, 1),
(294, 'TEXT', '**考点**：考察自我认知、岗位匹配度、改进意识。\n\n**优点**：选1-2个与岗位强相关的，用具体事例佐证。如\"执行力强，曾主导XX项目按期交付\"。\n\n**缺点**：说真实但非致命的，避免\"我太追求完美\"这类伪缺点。如\"公开表达经验不足\"。\n\n**改进**：给出可落地的行动，如\"主动争取汇报机会，已坚持每月做一次分享\"。\n\n**原则**：\n- 优点扣岗位需求，缺点不碰核心能力红线。\n- 缺点必须配改进措施，体现成长性。\n- 真诚具体，忌空泛套话。', NULL, 1),
(295, 'TEXT', '核心考点：动机真实性、岗位匹配度、公司认同感。\n\n1. **认同公司**：点出公司业务、产品、行业地位或文化中你真正认可的一点，避免空泛吹捧。\n2. **匹配岗位**：说明你的技能、经验与岗位要求高度契合，能快速上手并创造价值。\n3. **结合规划**：表达公司平台符合你的职业发展方向，你想在此长期成长。\n4. **差异化**：可提一个具体细节（如某产品、某技术、某价值观），体现你做过功课。\n\n答题结构：认可公司 + 我能贡献什么 + 我想获得什么成长。忌只谈公司好或只谈自己需要。', NULL, 1),
(296, 'TEXT', '1. 核心流程：长链→唯一短码→存储映射；访问短链→查映射→302重定向。\n2. 短码生成：可用自增ID转62进制，或哈希+冲突处理；需全局唯一、不可预测可选加随机盐。\n3. 存储：KV存储，短码为key，长链为value；量大时用Redis缓存热点，MySQL持久化。\n4. 高并发：读多写少，缓存+CDN+分库分表；写走发号器或分布式ID。\n5. 重定向：用302便于统计和后续修改；如需永久用301。\n6. 扩展：防刷、限流、过期清理、统计点击、自定义短码。', NULL, 1),
(297, 'TEXT', '1. 需求：单聊/群聊、在线状态、消息可靠投递、离线消息、多端同步。\n\n2. 架构：客户端通过 WebSocket 长连接接入网关层；网关无状态，用一致性哈希路由到同一用户连接。\n\n3. 存储：消息存 MySQL/Cassandra，按会话+时间分片；最近消息用 Redis 缓存；未读数、在线状态用 Redis。\n\n4. 投递：发送方消息先落库再推送；接收方在线则网关直推，离线则存离线表，上线拉取。\n\n5. 群聊：写扩散（小群）或读扩散（大群），用消息队列削峰异步投递。\n\n6. 可靠性：ACK 确认+重传、消息去重（seq/msgId）、有序性靠会话内递增序列号。\n\n7. 扩展：网关水平扩容，心跳保活，断线重连补拉增量消息。', NULL, 1),
(298, 'TEXT', '核心思路：层层过滤，把流量挡在数据库之前。\n\n1. **前端**：按钮置灰防重复提交；静态资源走 CDN。\n2. **网关/接入层**：限流（令牌桶）、黑名单、验证码削峰。\n3. **Redis 预扣库存**：用 Lua 脚本原子判断并扣减，库存不足直接返回，避免超卖。\n4. **异步下单**：扣减成功后发 MQ，异步落库创建订单，削峰填谷。\n5. **数据库**：库存字段加乐观锁/唯一索引兜底，防超卖。\n6. **兜底**：失败重试、幂等（订单号去重）、限购。\n\n要点：Redis 抗量、MQ 异步、DB 兜底，保证不超卖、高可用。', NULL, 1),
(299, 'TEXT', '1. 架构：客户端→路由层（一致性哈希）→缓存节点，节点间无共享，支持水平扩展。\n2. 数据分布：一致性哈希+虚拟节点，减少扩缩容时的数据迁移。\n3. 缓存策略：LRU/LFU 淘汰，TTL 过期，读多写少场景用 Cache-Aside。\n4. 高可用：主从复制+哨兵/集群选主，故障自动切换；多副本防单点。\n5. 一致性：最终一致，写时更新 DB 后删缓存（延迟双删），读时回填。\n6. 穿透/击穿/雪崩：布隆过滤器、互斥锁重建、过期时间加随机。\n7. 监控：命中率、延迟、内存、热点 key，支撑扩容与调优。', NULL, 1),
(300, 'TEXT', '1. 采集：Agent（Filebeat/Fluentd）收集日志，异步发送，本地磁盘缓冲防丢。\n2. 传输：Kafka 削峰解耦，按主题分区，保证高吞吐与顺序性。\n3. 存储：分冷热。热数据存 ES 供实时检索；冷数据压缩后入对象存储（S3/HDFS）降成本。\n4. 分析：实时用 Flink/Spark Streaming 做告警与聚合；离线跑批做统计。\n5. 查询：Kibana/Grafana 可视化，按时间+索引分片。\n6. 保障：限流、背压、副本容错、TTL 清理。', NULL, 1),
(301, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    int key;\n    int value;\n} Entry;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, target;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &target);\n    int *nums = (int *)malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &nums[i]);\n    }\n\n    Entry *map = (Entry *)malloc(n * sizeof(Entry));\n    int size = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int complement = target - nums[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\n            if (map[j].key == complement) {\n                printf(\"[%d,%d]\\n\", map[j].value, i);\n                free(nums);\n                free(map);\n                return 0;\n            }\n        }\n        map[size].key = nums[i];\n        map[size].value = i;\n        size++;\n    }\n\n    free(nums);\n    free(map);\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(301, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, target;\n    cin >> n >> target;\n    vector<int> nums(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> nums[i];\n    }\n    unordered_map<int, int> map;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int complement = target - nums[i];\n        if (map.find(complement) != map.end()) {\n            cout << \"[\" << map[complement] << \",\" << i << \"]\" << endl;\n            return 0;\n        }\n        map[nums[i]] = i;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(301, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int target = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] nums = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            nums[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n        Map<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int complement = target - nums[i];\n            if (map.containsKey(complement)) {\n                System.out.println(\"[\" + map.get(complement) + \",\" + i + \"]\");\n                return;\n            }\n            map.put(nums[i], i);\n        }\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(301, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n  input: process.stdin,\n  output: process.stdout\n});\n\nlet lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n  lines.push(line.trim());\n  if (lines.length === 2) {\n    const [n, target] = lines[0].split(\' \').map(Number);\n    const nums = lines[1].split(\' \').map(Number);\n    const map = new Map();\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      const complement = target - nums[i];\n      if (map.has(complement)) {\n        console.log(`[${map.get(complement)},${i}]`);\n        rl.close();\n        return;\n      }\n      map.set(nums[i], i);\n    }\n    rl.close();\n  }\n});', NULL, 1),
(301, 'PYTHON', 'n, target = map(int, input().split())\nnums = list(map(int, input().split()))\nseen = {}\nfor i, num in enumerate(nums):\n    complement = target - num\n    if complement in seen:\n        print(f\"[{seen[complement]},{i}]\")\n        break\n    seen[num] = i', NULL, 1),
(302, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint lengthOfLongestSubstring(char *s) {\n    int last[128];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 128; i++) {\n        last[i] = -1;\n    }\n    int maxLen = 0;\n    int left = 0;\n    int len = strlen(s);\n    for (int right = 0; right < len; right++) {\n        unsigned char c = (unsigned char)s[right];\n        if (last[c] >= left) {\n            left = last[c] + 1;\n        }\n        last[c] = right;\n        int curLen = right - left + 1;\n        if (curLen > maxLen) {\n            maxLen = curLen;\n        }\n    }\n    return maxLen;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    char s[1000000];\n    if (fgets(s, sizeof(s), stdin) != NULL) {\n        size_t len = strlen(s);\n        if (len > 0 && s[len - 1] == \'\\n\') {\n            s[len - 1] = \'\\0\';\n        }\n        printf(\"%d\\n\", lengthOfLongestSubstring(s));\n    }\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(302, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint lengthOfLongestSubstring(const string& s) {\n    int last[128];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 128; i++) {\n        last[i] = -1;\n    }\n    int maxLen = 0;\n    int left = 0;\n    for (int right = 0; right < (int)s.length(); right++) {\n        char c = s[right];\n        if (last[(int)c] >= left) {\n            left = last[(int)c] + 1;\n        }\n        last[(int)c] = right;\n        maxLen = max(maxLen, right - left + 1);\n    }\n    return maxLen;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    if (getline(cin, s)) {\n        cout << lengthOfLongestSubstring(s) << endl;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(302, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (scanner.hasNextLine()) {\n            String s = scanner.nextLine();\n            System.out.println(lengthOfLongestSubstring(s));\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {\n        int[] last = new int[128];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 128; i++) {\n            last[i] = -1;\n        }\n        int maxLen = 0;\n        int left = 0;\n        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {\n            char c = s.charAt(right);\n            if (last[c] >= left) {\n                left = last[c] + 1;\n            }\n            last[c] = right;\n            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, right - left + 1);\n        }\n        return maxLen;\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(302, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nrl.on(\'line\', (s) => {\n    console.log(lengthOfLongestSubstring(s));\n    rl.close();\n});\n\nfunction lengthOfLongestSubstring(s) {\n    const last = new Array(128).fill(-1);\n    let maxLen = 0;\n    let left = 0;\n    for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {\n        const c = s.charCodeAt(right);\n        if (last[c] >= left) {\n            left = last[c] + 1;\n        }\n        last[c] = right;\n        maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, right - left + 1);\n    }\n    return maxLen;\n}', NULL, 1),
(302, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\ndef lengthOfLongestSubstring(s):\n    last = [-1] * 128\n    maxLen = 0\n    left = 0\n    for right, c in enumerate(s):\n        code = ord(c)\n        if last[code] >= left:\n            left = last[code] + 1\n        last[code] = right\n        maxLen = max(maxLen, right - left + 1)\n    return maxLen\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip(\'\\n\')\n    print(lengthOfLongestSubstring(s))', NULL, 1),
(303, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint expand(char *s, int left, int right, int n) {\n    while (left >= 0 && right < n && s[left] == s[right]) {\n        left--;\n        right++;\n    }\n    return right - left - 1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    char s[100000];\n    if (!fgets(s, sizeof(s), stdin)) return 0;\n    int n = strlen(s);\n    if (n > 0 && s[n - 1] == \'\\n\') {\n        s[n - 1] = \'\\0\';\n        n--;\n    }\n    if (n == 0) {\n        printf(\"\\n\");\n        return 0;\n    }\n    int start = 0, end = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int len1 = expand(s, i, i, n);\n        int len2 = expand(s, i, i + 1, n);\n        int len = len1 > len2 ? len1 : len2;\n        if (len > end - start + 1) {\n            start = i - (len - 1) / 2;\n            end = i + len / 2;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {\n        putchar(s[i]);\n    }\n    putchar(\'\\n\');\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(303, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint expand(const string& s, int left, int right) {\n    while (left >= 0 && right < (int)s.length() && s[left] == s[right]) {\n        left--;\n        right++;\n    }\n    return right - left - 1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    if (!getline(cin, s)) return 0;\n    if (s.empty()) {\n        cout << \"\" << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    int start = 0, end = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)s.length(); i++) {\n        int len1 = expand(s, i, i);\n        int len2 = expand(s, i, i + 1);\n        int len = max(len1, len2);\n        if (len > end - start + 1) {\n            start = i - (len - 1) / 2;\n            end = i + len / 2;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << s.substr(start, end - start + 1) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(303, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (!sc.hasNextLine()) return;\n        String s = sc.nextLine();\n        if (s == null || s.length() == 0) {\n            System.out.println(\"\");\n            return;\n        }\n        int start = 0, end = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n            int len1 = expand(s, i, i);\n            int len2 = expand(s, i, i + 1);\n            int len = Math.max(len1, len2);\n            if (len > end - start + 1) {\n                start = i - (len - 1) / 2;\n                end = i + len / 2;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(s.substring(start, end + 1));\n    }\n\n    private static int expand(String s, int left, int right) {\n        while (left >= 0 && right < s.length() && s.charAt(left) == s.charAt(right)) {\n            left--;\n            right++;\n        }\n        return right - left - 1;\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(303, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nrl.on(\'line\', (s) => {\n    if (s === null || s.length === 0) {\n        console.log(\"\");\n        rl.close();\n        return;\n    }\n    let start = 0, end = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n        let len1 = expand(s, i, i);\n        let len2 = expand(s, i, i + 1);\n        let len = Math.max(len1, len2);\n        if (len > end - start + 1) {\n            start = i - Math.floor((len - 1) / 2);\n            end = i + Math.floor(len / 2);\n        }\n    }\n    console.log(s.substring(start, end + 1));\n    rl.close();\n});\n\nfunction expand(s, left, right) {\n    while (left >= 0 && right < s.length && s[left] === s[right]) {\n        left--;\n        right++;\n    }\n    return right - left - 1;\n}', NULL, 1),
(303, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\ndef expand(s, left, right):\n    while left >= 0 and right < len(s) and s[left] == s[right]:\n        left -= 1\n        right += 1\n    return right - left - 1\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip(\'\\n\')\n    if not s:\n        print(\"\")\n        return\n    start, end = 0, 0\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        len1 = expand(s, i, i)\n        len2 = expand(s, i, i + 1)\n        length = max(len1, len2)\n        if length > end - start + 1:\n            start = i - (length - 1) // 2\n            end = i + length // 2\n    print(s[start:end + 1])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(304, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    struct ListNode *next;\n};\n\nstruct ListNode* reverseList(struct ListNode* head) {\n    struct ListNode* prev = NULL;\n    struct ListNode* curr = head;\n    while (curr != NULL) {\n        struct ListNode* nextTemp = curr->next;\n        curr->next = prev;\n        prev = curr;\n        curr = nextTemp;\n    }\n    return prev;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    char input[100000];\n    if (fgets(input, sizeof(input), stdin) == NULL) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    size_t len = strlen(input);\n    while (len > 0 && (input[len - 1] == \'\\n\' || input[len - 1] == \'\\r\')) {\n        input[--len] = \'\\0\';\n    }\n\n    struct ListNode dummy;\n    dummy.val = 0;\n    dummy.next = NULL;\n    struct ListNode* tail = &dummy;\n\n    char* token = strtok(input, \"->\");\n    while (token != NULL) {\n        if (strcmp(token, \"NULL\") == 0) {\n            break;\n        }\n        int val = atoi(token);\n        struct ListNode* node = (struct ListNode*)malloc(sizeof(struct ListNode));\n        node->val = val;\n        node->next = NULL;\n        tail->next = node;\n        tail = node;\n        token = strtok(NULL, \"->\");\n    }\n\n    struct ListNode* reversed = reverseList(dummy.next);\n\n    struct ListNode* curr = reversed;\n    while (curr != NULL) {\n        printf(\"%d->\", curr->val);\n        curr = curr->next;\n    }\n    printf(\"NULL\\n\");\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(304, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    ListNode* next;\n    ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nListNode* reverseList(ListNode* head) {\n    ListNode* prev = nullptr;\n    ListNode* curr = head;\n    while (curr != nullptr) {\n        ListNode* nextTemp = curr->next;\n        curr->next = prev;\n        prev = curr;\n        curr = nextTemp;\n    }\n    return prev;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    std::string input;\n    std::getline(std::cin, input);\n\n    ListNode dummy(0);\n    ListNode* tail = &dummy;\n\n    size_t pos = 0;\n    while (pos < input.size()) {\n        size_t nextPos = input.find(\"->\", pos);\n        std::string part;\n        if (nextPos == std::string::npos) {\n            part = input.substr(pos);\n            pos = input.size();\n        } else {\n            part = input.substr(pos, nextPos - pos);\n            pos = nextPos + 2;\n        }\n\n        if (part == \"NULL\") {\n            break;\n        }\n\n        int val = std::stoi(part);\n        tail->next = new ListNode(val);\n        tail = tail->next;\n    }\n\n    ListNode* reversed = reverseList(dummy.next);\n\n    std::ostringstream oss;\n    ListNode* curr = reversed;\n    while (curr != nullptr) {\n        oss << curr->val << \"->\";\n        curr = curr->next;\n    }\n    oss << \"NULL\";\n    std::cout << oss.str() << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(304, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class ListNode {\n        int val;\n        ListNode next;\n        ListNode(int val) {\n            this.val = val;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {\n        ListNode prev = null;\n        ListNode curr = head;\n        while (curr != null) {\n            ListNode nextTemp = curr.next;\n            curr.next = prev;\n            prev = curr;\n            curr = nextTemp;\n        }\n        return prev;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String input = scanner.nextLine().trim();\n        String[] parts = input.split(\"->\");\n        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);\n        ListNode tail = dummy;\n        for (String part : parts) {\n            if (part.equals(\"NULL\")) {\n                break;\n            }\n            int val = Integer.parseInt(part);\n            tail.next = new ListNode(val);\n            tail = tail.next;\n        }\n\n        ListNode reversed = reverseList(dummy.next);\n\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        ListNode curr = reversed;\n        while (curr != null) {\n            sb.append(curr.val).append(\"->\");\n            curr = curr.next;\n        }\n        sb.append(\"NULL\");\n        System.out.println(sb.toString());\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(304, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nclass ListNode {\n    constructor(val) {\n        this.val = val;\n        this.next = null;\n    }\n}\n\nfunction reverseList(head) {\n    let prev = null;\n    let curr = head;\n    while (curr !== null) {\n        let nextTemp = curr.next;\n        curr.next = prev;\n        prev = curr;\n        curr = nextTemp;\n    }\n    return prev;\n}\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    const input = line.trim();\n    const parts = input.split(\'->\');\n    const dummy = new ListNode(0);\n    let tail = dummy;\n    for (const part of parts) {\n        if (part === \'NULL\') {\n            break;\n        }\n        const val = parseInt(part, 10);\n        tail.next = new ListNode(val);\n        tail = tail.next;\n    }\n\n    const reversed = reverseList(dummy.next);\n\n    let sb = \'\';\n    let curr = reversed;\n    while (curr !== null) {\n        sb += curr.val + \'->\';\n        curr = curr.next;\n    }\n    sb += \'NULL\';\n    console.log(sb);\n    rl.close();\n});', NULL, 1),
(304, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\nclass ListNode:\n    def __init__(self, val):\n        self.val = val\n        self.next = None\n\ndef reverseList(head):\n    prev = None\n    curr = head\n    while curr is not None:\n        nextTemp = curr.next\n        curr.next = prev\n        prev = curr\n        curr = nextTemp\n    return prev\n\ndef main():\n    input_str = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    parts = input_str.split(\"->\")\n    dummy = ListNode(0)\n    tail = dummy\n    for part in parts:\n        if part == \"NULL\":\n            break\n        val = int(part)\n        tail.next = ListNode(val)\n        tail = tail.next\n\n    reversed_head = reverseList(dummy.next)\n\n    sb = []\n    curr = reversed_head\n    while curr is not None:\n        sb.append(str(curr.val))\n        sb.append(\"->\")\n        curr = curr.next\n    sb.append(\"NULL\")\n    print(\"\".join(sb))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(305, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    struct ListNode *next;\n};\n\nstruct ListNode* parseList(char *line) {\n    if (line == NULL) return NULL;\n    while (*line == \' \' || *line == \'\\t\' || *line == \'\\n\' || *line == \'\\r\') line++;\n    if (*line == \'\\0\' || strcmp(line, \"NULL\") == 0) return NULL;\n\n    struct ListNode dummy;\n    dummy.val = 0;\n    dummy.next = NULL;\n    struct ListNode *cur = &dummy;\n\n    char *token = strtok(line, \"->\");\n    while (token != NULL) {\n        while (*token == \' \' || *token == \'\\t\') token++;\n        if (strcmp(token, \"NULL\") == 0) break;\n        struct ListNode *node = (struct ListNode*)malloc(sizeof(struct ListNode));\n        node->val = atoi(token);\n        node->next = NULL;\n        cur->next = node;\n        cur = cur->next;\n        token = strtok(NULL, \"->\");\n    }\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nstruct ListNode* mergeTwoLists(struct ListNode* l1, struct ListNode* l2) {\n    struct ListNode dummy;\n    dummy.val = 0;\n    dummy.next = NULL;\n    struct ListNode *cur = &dummy;\n\n    while (l1 != NULL && l2 != NULL) {\n        if (l1->val <= l2->val) {\n            cur->next = l1;\n            l1 = l1->next;\n        } else {\n            cur->next = l2;\n            l2 = l2->next;\n        }\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    if (l1 != NULL) cur->next = l1;\n    if (l2 != NULL) cur->next = l2;\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    char line1[10000];\n    char line2[10000];\n\n    if (fgets(line1, sizeof(line1), stdin) == NULL) return 0;\n    if (fgets(line2, sizeof(line2), stdin) == NULL) return 0;\n\n    line1[strcspn(line1, \"\\n\")] = \'\\0\';\n    line2[strcspn(line2, \"\\n\")] = \'\\0\';\n\n    struct ListNode *l1 = parseList(line1);\n    struct ListNode *l2 = parseList(line2);\n\n    struct ListNode *merged = mergeTwoLists(l1, l2);\n\n    struct ListNode *cur = merged;\n    while (cur != NULL) {\n        printf(\"%d\", cur->val);\n        if (cur->next != NULL) {\n            printf(\"->\");\n        }\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(305, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    ListNode* next;\n    ListNode(int val) : val(val), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nListNode* parseList(const std::string& line) {\n    if (line.empty()) {\n        return nullptr;\n    }\n    std::string s = line;\n    // trim\n    size_t start = s.find_first_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\");\n    if (start == std::string::npos) return nullptr;\n    size_t end = s.find_last_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\");\n    s = s.substr(start, end - start + 1);\n\n    if (s.empty() || s == \"NULL\") {\n        return nullptr;\n    }\n    if (s.size() >= 6 && s.substr(s.size() - 6) == \"->NULL\") {\n        s = s.substr(0, s.size() - 6);\n    } else if (s.size() >= 4 && s.substr(s.size() - 4) == \"NULL\") {\n        s = s.substr(0, s.size() - 4);\n        if (s.size() >= 2 && s.substr(s.size() - 2) == \"->\") {\n            s = s.substr(0, s.size() - 2);\n        }\n    }\n    if (s.empty()) {\n        return nullptr;\n    }\n\n    ListNode dummy(0);\n    ListNode* cur = &dummy;\n    std::stringstream ss(s);\n    std::string part;\n    while (std::getline(ss, part, \'-\')) {\n        // getline with \'-\' delimiter will split \"1->2\" into \"1\" and \">2\"\n        // Better to manually parse\n    }\n\n    // Manual parse by \"->\"\n    size_t pos = 0;\n    while (pos < s.size()) {\n        size_t nextPos = s.find(\"->\", pos);\n        std::string token;\n        if (nextPos == std::string::npos) {\n            token = s.substr(pos);\n            pos = s.size();\n        } else {\n            token = s.substr(pos, nextPos - pos);\n            pos = nextPos + 2;\n        }\n        // trim token\n        size_t ts = token.find_first_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\");\n        if (ts == std::string::npos) continue;\n        size_t te = token.find_last_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\");\n        token = token.substr(ts, te - ts + 1);\n        if (token.empty()) continue;\n        cur->next = new ListNode(std::stoi(token));\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nListNode* mergeTwoLists(ListNode* l1, ListNode* l2) {\n    ListNode dummy(0);\n    ListNode* cur = &dummy;\n    while (l1 != nullptr && l2 != nullptr) {\n        if (l1->val <= l2->val) {\n            cur->next = l1;\n            l1 = l1->next;\n        } else {\n            cur->next = l2;\n            l2 = l2->next;\n        }\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    if (l1 != nullptr) {\n        cur->next = l1;\n    } else {\n        cur->next = l2;\n    }\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::string line1, line2;\n    std::getline(std::cin, line1);\n    std::getline(std::cin, line2);\n\n    ListNode* l1 = parseList(line1);\n    ListNode* l2 = parseList(line2);\n\n    ListNode* merged = mergeTwoLists(l1, l2);\n\n    std::string result;\n    ListNode* cur = merged;\n    while (cur != nullptr) {\n        result += std::to_string(cur->val);\n        if (cur->next != nullptr) {\n            result += \"->\";\n        }\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    std::cout << result;\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(305, 'JAVA', 'import java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class ListNode {\n        int val;\n        ListNode next;\n        ListNode(int val) {\n            this.val = val;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line1 = br.readLine();\n        String line2 = br.readLine();\n\n        ListNode l1 = parseList(line1);\n        ListNode l2 = parseList(line2);\n\n        ListNode merged = mergeTwoLists(l1, l2);\n\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        ListNode cur = merged;\n        while (cur != null) {\n            sb.append(cur.val);\n            if (cur.next != null) {\n                sb.append(\"->\");\n            }\n            cur = cur.next;\n        }\n        System.out.println(sb.toString());\n    }\n\n    private static ListNode parseList(String line) {\n        if (line == null) return null;\n        line = line.trim();\n        if (line.isEmpty() || line.equals(\"NULL\")) return null;\n\n        String[] parts = line.split(\"->\");\n        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);\n        ListNode cur = dummy;\n        for (String part : parts) {\n            part = part.trim();\n            if (part.equals(\"NULL\")) break;\n            cur.next = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(part));\n            cur = cur.next;\n        }\n        return dummy.next;\n    }\n\n    private static ListNode mergeTwoLists(ListNode l1, ListNode l2) {\n        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);\n        ListNode cur = dummy;\n        while (l1 != null && l2 != null) {\n            if (l1.val <= l2.val) {\n                cur.next = l1;\n                l1 = l1.next;\n            } else {\n                cur.next = l2;\n                l2 = l2.next;\n            }\n            cur = cur.next;\n        }\n        if (l1 != null) cur.next = l1;\n        if (l2 != null) cur.next = l2;\n        return dummy.next;\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(305, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nclass ListNode {\n    constructor(val) {\n        this.val = val;\n        this.next = null;\n    }\n}\n\nfunction parseList(line) {\n    if (line === null || line === undefined) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    line = line.trim();\n    if (line === \'\' || line === \'NULL\') {\n        return null;\n    }\n    if (line.endsWith(\'->NULL\')) {\n        line = line.substring(0, line.length - 6);\n    } else if (line.endsWith(\'NULL\')) {\n        line = line.substring(0, line.length - 4);\n        if (line.endsWith(\'->\')) {\n            line = line.substring(0, line.length - 2);\n        }\n    }\n    if (line === \'\') {\n        return null;\n    }\n    const parts = line.split(\'->\');\n    const dummy = new ListNode(0);\n    let cur = dummy;\n    for (let part of parts) {\n        part = part.trim();\n        if (part === \'\') {\n            continue;\n        }\n        cur.next = new ListNode(parseInt(part, 10));\n        cur = cur.next;\n    }\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nfunction mergeTwoLists(l1, l2) {\n    const dummy = new ListNode(0);\n    let cur = dummy;\n    while (l1 !== null && l2 !== null) {\n        if (l1.val <= l2.val) {\n            cur.next = l1;\n            l1 = l1.next;\n        } else {\n            cur.next = l2;\n            l2 = l2.next;\n        }\n        cur = cur.next;\n    }\n    if (l1 !== null) {\n        cur.next = l1;\n    } else {\n        cur.next = l2;\n    }\n    return dummy.next;\n}\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nconst lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    lines.push(line);\n    if (lines.length === 2) {\n        rl.close();\n    }\n});\n\nrl.on(\'close\', () => {\n    const l1 = parseList(lines[0]);\n    const l2 = parseList(lines[1]);\n    const merged = mergeTwoLists(l1, l2);\n    let sb = \'\';\n    let cur = merged;\n    while (cur !== null) {\n        sb += cur.val;\n        if (cur.next !== null) {\n            sb += \'->\';\n        }\n        cur = cur.next;\n    }\n    process.stdout.write(sb);\n});', NULL, 1),
(305, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\nclass ListNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0):\n        self.val = val\n        self.next = None\n\ndef parse_list(line):\n    if line is None:\n        return None\n    line = line.strip()\n    if not line or line == \"NULL\":\n        return None\n    if line.endswith(\"->NULL\"):\n        line = line[:-6]\n    elif line.endswith(\"NULL\"):\n        line = line[:-4]\n        if line.endswith(\"->\"):\n            line = line[:-2]\n    if not line:\n        return None\n    parts = line.split(\"->\")\n    dummy = ListNode(0)\n    cur = dummy\n    for part in parts:\n        part = part.strip()\n        if not part:\n            continue\n        cur.next = ListNode(int(part))\n        cur = cur.next\n    return dummy.next\n\ndef merge_two_lists(l1, l2):\n    dummy = ListNode(0)\n    cur = dummy\n    while l1 is not None and l2 is not None:\n        if l1.val <= l2.val:\n            cur.next = l1\n            l1 = l1.next\n        else:\n            cur.next = l2\n            l2 = l2.next\n        cur = cur.next\n    if l1 is not None:\n        cur.next = l1\n    else:\n        cur.next = l2\n    return dummy.next\n\ndef main():\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    line1 = lines[0] if len(lines) > 0 else None\n    line2 = lines[1] if len(lines) > 1 else None\n\n    l1 = parse_list(line1)\n    l2 = parse_list(line2)\n\n    merged = merge_two_lists(l1, l2)\n\n    result = []\n    cur = merged\n    while cur is not None:\n        result.append(str(cur.val))\n        cur = cur.next\n    sys.stdout.write(\"->\".join(result))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(306, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct Node {\n    int key, value;\n    struct Node *prev, *next;\n} Node;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    int capacity;\n    int size;\n    Node **map;\n    int mapSize;\n    Node *head, *tail;\n} LRUCache;\n\nstatic unsigned int hash(int key, int mod) {\n    unsigned int x = (unsigned int)key;\n    x = ((x >> 16) ^ x) * 0x45d9f3b;\n    x = ((x >> 16) ^ x) * 0x45d9f3b;\n    x = (x >> 16) ^ x;\n    return x % (unsigned int)mod;\n}\n\nstatic Node* mapGet(LRUCache *cache, int key) {\n    unsigned int idx = hash(key, cache->mapSize);\n    Node *cur = cache->map[idx];\n    while (cur) {\n        if (cur->key == key) return cur;\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n    return NULL;\n}\n\nstatic void mapPut(LRUCache *cache, int key, Node *node) {\n    unsigned int idx = hash(key, cache->mapSize);\n    node->next = cache->map[idx];\n    cache->map[idx] = node;\n}\n\nstatic void mapRemove(LRUCache *cache, int key) {\n    unsigned int idx = hash(key, cache->mapSize);\n    Node *cur = cache->map[idx];\n    Node *prev = NULL;\n    while (cur) {\n        if (cur->key == key) {\n            if (prev) prev->next = cur->next;\n            else cache->map[idx] = cur->next;\n            return;\n        }\n        prev = cur;\n        cur = cur->next;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void addToHead(LRUCache *cache, Node *node) {\n    node->prev = cache->head;\n    node->next = cache->head->next;\n    cache->head->next->prev = node;\n    cache->head->next = node;\n}\n\nstatic void removeNode(LRUCache *cache, Node *node) {\n    (void)cache;\n    node->prev->next = node->next;\n    node->next->prev = node->prev;\n}\n\nstatic void moveToHead(LRUCache *cache, Node *node) {\n    removeNode(cache, node);\n    addToHead(cache, node);\n}\n\nstatic Node* removeTail(LRUCache *cache) {\n    Node *node = cache->tail->prev;\n    removeNode(cache, node);\n    return node;\n}\n\nstatic LRUCache* LRUCacheCreate(int capacity) {\n    LRUCache *cache = (LRUCache*)malloc(sizeof(LRUCache));\n    cache->capacity = capacity;\n    cache->size = 0;\n    cache->mapSize = capacity * 4 + 17;\n    cache->map = (Node**)calloc(cache->mapSize, sizeof(Node*));\n    cache->head = (Node*)malloc(sizeof(Node));\n    cache->tail = (Node*)malloc(sizeof(Node));\n    cache->head->key = -1;\n    cache->head->value = -1;\n    cache->tail->key = -1;\n    cache->tail->value = -1;\n    cache->head->prev = NULL;\n    cache->head->next = cache->tail;\n    cache->tail->prev = cache->head;\n    cache->tail->next = NULL;\n    return cache;\n}\n\nstatic int LRUCacheGet(LRUCache *cache, int key) {\n    Node *node = mapGet(cache, key);\n    if (!node) return -1;\n    moveToHead(cache, node);\n    return node->value;\n}\n\nstatic void LRUCachePut(LRUCache *cache, int key, int value) {\n    Node *node = mapGet(cache, key);\n    if (node) {\n        node->value = value;\n        moveToHead(cache, node);\n    } else {\n        if (cache->size == cache->capacity) {\n            Node *removed = removeTail(cache);\n            mapRemove(cache, removed->key);\n            free(removed);\n            cache->size--;\n        }\n        Node *newNode = (Node*)malloc(sizeof(Node));\n        newNode->key = key;\n        newNode->value = value;\n        newNode->prev = NULL;\n        newNode->next = NULL;\n        mapPut(cache, key, newNode);\n        addToHead(cache, newNode);\n        cache->size++;\n    }\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int capacity, m;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &capacity) != 1) return 0;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &m) != 1) return 0;\n\n    LRUCache *cache = LRUCacheCreate(capacity);\n\n    char op[16];\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n        if (scanf(\"%15s\", op) != 1) break;\n        if (strcmp(op, \"put\") == 0) {\n            int key, value;\n            scanf(\"%d %d\", &key, &value);\n            LRUCachePut(cache, key, value);\n        } else if (strcmp(op, \"get\") == 0) {\n            int key;\n            scanf(\"%d\", &key);\n            printf(\"%d\\n\", LRUCacheGet(cache, key));\n        }\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(306, 'CPP', '#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass LRUCache {\nprivate:\n    struct Node {\n        int key, value;\n        Node *prev, *next;\n        Node(int k, int v) : key(k), value(v), prev(nullptr), next(nullptr) {}\n    };\n\n    int capacity;\n    unordered_map<int, Node*> mp;\n    Node *head, *tail;\n\n    void addToHead(Node* node) {\n        node->prev = head;\n        node->next = head->next;\n        head->next->prev = node;\n        head->next = node;\n    }\n\n    void removeNode(Node* node) {\n        node->prev->next = node->next;\n        node->next->prev = node->prev;\n    }\n\n    void moveToHead(Node* node) {\n        removeNode(node);\n        addToHead(node);\n    }\n\n    Node* removeTail() {\n        Node* node = tail->prev;\n        removeNode(node);\n        return node;\n    }\n\npublic:\n    LRUCache(int capacity) : capacity(capacity) {\n        head = new Node(-1, -1);\n        tail = new Node(-1, -1);\n        head->next = tail;\n        tail->prev = head;\n    }\n\n    int get(int key) {\n        auto it = mp.find(key);\n        if (it == mp.end()) return -1;\n        Node* node = it->second;\n        moveToHead(node);\n        return node->value;\n    }\n\n    void put(int key, int value) {\n        auto it = mp.find(key);\n        if (it != mp.end()) {\n            Node* node = it->second;\n            node->value = value;\n            moveToHead(node);\n        } else {\n            if ((int)mp.size() == capacity) {\n                Node* removed = removeTail();\n                mp.erase(removed->key);\n                delete removed;\n            }\n            Node* newNode = new Node(key, value);\n            mp[key] = newNode;\n            addToHead(newNode);\n        }\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int capacity;\n    cin >> capacity;\n    int m;\n    cin >> m;\n\n    LRUCache cache(capacity);\n    string op;\n    while (m--) {\n        cin >> op;\n        if (op == \"put\") {\n            int key, value;\n            cin >> key >> value;\n            cache.put(key, value);\n        } else if (op == \"get\") {\n            int key;\n            cin >> key;\n            cout << cache.get(key) << \'\\n\';\n        }\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(306, 'JAVA', 'import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class LRUCache {\n        class Node {\n            int key, value;\n            Node prev, next;\n            Node(int k, int v) {\n                key = k;\n                value = v;\n            }\n        }\n\n        private int capacity;\n        private Map<Integer, Node> map;\n        private Node head, tail;\n\n        public LRUCache(int capacity) {\n            this.capacity = capacity;\n            this.map = new HashMap<>();\n            head = new Node(-1, -1);\n            tail = new Node(-1, -1);\n            head.next = tail;\n            tail.prev = head;\n        }\n\n        public int get(int key) {\n            Node node = map.get(key);\n            if (node == null) return -1;\n            moveToHead(node);\n            return node.value;\n        }\n\n        public void put(int key, int value) {\n            Node node = map.get(key);\n            if (node != null) {\n                node.value = value;\n                moveToHead(node);\n            } else {\n                if (map.size() == capacity) {\n                    Node removed = removeTail();\n                    map.remove(removed.key);\n                }\n                Node newNode = new Node(key, value);\n                map.put(key, newNode);\n                addToHead(newNode);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void addToHead(Node node) {\n            node.prev = head;\n            node.next = head.next;\n            head.next.prev = node;\n            head.next = node;\n        }\n\n        private void removeNode(Node node) {\n            node.prev.next = node.next;\n            node.next.prev = node.prev;\n        }\n\n        private void moveToHead(Node node) {\n            removeNode(node);\n            addToHead(node);\n        }\n\n        private Node removeTail() {\n            Node node = tail.prev;\n            removeNode(node);\n            return node;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int capacity = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        int m = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        LRUCache cache = new LRUCache(capacity);\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            String line = br.readLine().trim();\n            if (line.isEmpty()) continue;\n            String[] parts = line.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            if (parts[0].equals(\"put\")) {\n                int key = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n                int value = Integer.parseInt(parts[2]);\n                cache.put(key, value);\n            } else if (parts[0].equals(\"get\")) {\n                int key = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n                sb.append(cache.get(key)).append(\'\\n\');\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(306, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nclass Node {\n    constructor(key, value) {\n        this.key = key;\n        this.value = value;\n        this.prev = null;\n        this.next = null;\n    }\n}\n\nclass LRUCache {\n    constructor(capacity) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.map = new Map();\n        this.head = new Node(-1, -1);\n        this.tail = new Node(-1, -1);\n        this.head.next = this.tail;\n        this.tail.prev = this.head;\n    }\n\n    get(key) {\n        const node = this.map.get(key);\n        if (node === undefined) return -1;\n        this.moveToHead(node);\n        return node.value;\n    }\n\n    put(key, value) {\n        const node = this.map.get(key);\n        if (node !== undefined) {\n            node.value = value;\n            this.moveToHead(node);\n        } else {\n            if (this.map.size === this.capacity) {\n                const removed = this.removeTail();\n                this.map.delete(removed.key);\n            }\n            const newNode = new Node(key, value);\n            this.map.set(key, newNode);\n            this.addToHead(newNode);\n        }\n    }\n\n    addToHead(node) {\n        node.prev = this.head;\n        node.next = this.head.next;\n        this.head.next.prev = node;\n        this.head.next = node;\n    }\n\n    removeNode(node) {\n        node.prev.next = node.next;\n        node.next.prev = node.prev;\n    }\n\n    moveToHead(node) {\n        this.removeNode(node);\n        this.addToHead(node);\n    }\n\n    removeTail() {\n        const node = this.tail.prev;\n        this.removeNode(node);\n        return node;\n    }\n}\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout,\n    terminal: false\n});\n\nlet lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    lines.push(line.trim());\n});\n\nrl.on(\'close\', () => {\n    let idx = 0;\n    const capacity = parseInt(lines[idx++]);\n    const m = parseInt(lines[idx++]);\n    const cache = new LRUCache(capacity);\n    const output = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n        const line = lines[idx++];\n        if (!line) continue;\n        const parts = line.split(/\\s+/);\n        if (parts[0] === \'put\') {\n            const key = parseInt(parts[1]);\n            const value = parseInt(parts[2]);\n            cache.put(key, value);\n        } else if (parts[0] === \'get\') {\n            const key = parseInt(parts[1]);\n            output.push(cache.get(key));\n        }\n    }\n    process.stdout.write(output.join(\'\\n\') + (output.length ? \'\\n\' : \'\'));\n});', NULL, 1),
(306, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\nclass Node:\n    __slots__ = (\'key\', \'value\', \'prev\', \'next\')\n    def __init__(self, k, v):\n        self.key = k\n        self.value = v\n        self.prev = None\n        self.next = None\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.map = {}\n        self.head = Node(-1, -1)\n        self.tail = Node(-1, -1)\n        self.head.next = self.tail\n        self.tail.prev = self.head\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        node = self.map.get(key)\n        if node is None:\n            return -1\n        self.moveToHead(node)\n        return node.value\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        node = self.map.get(key)\n        if node is not None:\n            node.value = value\n            self.moveToHead(node)\n        else:\n            if len(self.map) == self.capacity:\n                removed = self.removeTail()\n                del self.map[removed.key]\n            newNode = Node(key, value)\n            self.map[key] = newNode\n            self.addToHead(newNode)\n\n    def addToHead(self, node):\n        node.prev = self.head\n        node.next = self.head.next\n        self.head.next.prev = node\n        self.head.next = node\n\n    def removeNode(self, node):\n        node.prev.next = node.next\n        node.next.prev = node.prev\n\n    def moveToHead(self, node):\n        self.removeNode(node)\n        self.addToHead(node)\n\n    def removeTail(self):\n        node = self.tail.prev\n        self.removeNode(node)\n        return node\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    idx = 0\n    capacity = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    m = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    cache = LRUCache(capacity)\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(m):\n        op = data[idx]; idx += 1\n        if op == \'put\':\n            key = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n            value = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n            cache.put(key, value)\n        elif op == \'get\':\n            key = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n            out.append(str(cache.get(key)))\n    sys.stdout.write(\'\\n\'.join(out) + (\'\\n\' if out else \'\'))\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(307, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\nbool isValid(const char *s) {\n    char stack[10000];\n    int top = -1;\n    for (int i = 0; s[i] != \'\\0\'; i++) {\n        char c = s[i];\n        if (c == \'(\' || c == \'{\' || c == \'[\') {\n            stack[++top] = c;\n        } else {\n            if (top == -1) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            char t = stack[top--];\n            if ((c == \')\' && t != \'(\') ||\n                (c == \'}\' && t != \'{\') ||\n                (c == \']\' && t != \'[\')) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return top == -1;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    char s[10000];\n    if (fgets(s, sizeof(s), stdin) == NULL) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    size_t len = strlen(s);\n    if (len > 0 && s[len - 1] == \'\\n\') {\n        s[len - 1] = \'\\0\';\n    }\n    if (isValid(s)) {\n        printf(\"true\\n\");\n    } else {\n        printf(\"false\\n\");\n    }\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(307, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <stack>\nusing namespace std;\n\nbool isValid(const string& s) {\n    stack<char> st;\n    for (char c : s) {\n        if (c == \'(\' || c == \'{\' || c == \'[\') {\n            st.push(c);\n        } else {\n            if (st.empty()) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            char top = st.top();\n            st.pop();\n            if ((c == \')\' && top != \'(\') ||\n                (c == \'}\' && top != \'{\') ||\n                (c == \']\' && top != \'[\')) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return st.empty();\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    if (!getline(cin, s)) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    cout << (isValid(s) ? \"true\" : \"false\") << endl;\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(307, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (!sc.hasNextLine()) {\n            return;\n        }\n        String s = sc.nextLine();\n        System.out.println(isValid(s));\n    }\n\n    public static boolean isValid(String s) {\n        Deque<Character> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\n            if (c == \'(\' || c == \'{\' || c == \'[\') {\n                stack.push(c);\n            } else {\n                if (stack.isEmpty()) {\n                    return false;\n                }\n                char top = stack.pop();\n                if ((c == \')\' && top != \'(\') ||\n                    (c == \'}\' && top != \'{\') ||\n                    (c == \']\' && top != \'[\')) {\n                    return false;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return stack.isEmpty();\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(307, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nrl.on(\'line\', (s) => {\n    console.log(isValid(s));\n    rl.close();\n});\n\nfunction isValid(s) {\n    const stack = [];\n    for (const c of s) {\n        if (c === \'(\' || c === \'{\' || c === \'[\') {\n            stack.push(c);\n        } else {\n            if (stack.length === 0) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            const top = stack.pop();\n            if ((c === \')\' && top !== \'(\') ||\n                (c === \'}\' && top !== \'{\') ||\n                (c === \']\' && top !== \'[\')) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return stack.length === 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(307, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\ndef isValid(s: str) -> bool:\n    stack = []\n    for c in s:\n        if c in \'({[\':\n            stack.append(c)\n        else:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            top = stack.pop()\n            if (c == \')\' and top != \'(\') or \\\n               (c == \'}\' and top != \'{\') or \\\n               (c == \']\' and top != \'[\'):\n                return False\n    return not stack\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip(\'\\n\')\n    print(\"true\" if isValid(s) else \"false\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(308, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint cmp(const void *a, const void *b) {\n    return (*(int *)a - *(int *)b);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int *nums = (int *)malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &nums[i]);\n    }\n    qsort(nums, n, sizeof(int), cmp);\n\n    int **res = (int **)malloc(n * n * sizeof(int *));\n    int resSize = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n        if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;\n        int left = i + 1, right = n - 1;\n        while (left < right) {\n            int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];\n            if (sum == 0) {\n                res[resSize] = (int *)malloc(3 * sizeof(int));\n                res[resSize][0] = nums[i];\n                res[resSize][1] = nums[left];\n                res[resSize][2] = nums[right];\n                resSize++;\n                while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left + 1]) left++;\n                while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right - 1]) right--;\n                left++;\n                right--;\n            } else if (sum < 0) {\n                left++;\n            } else {\n                right--;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"[\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < resSize; i++) {\n        printf(\"[%d,%d,%d]\", res[i][0], res[i][1], res[i][2]);\n        if (i != resSize - 1) printf(\",\");\n    }\n    printf(\"]\\n\");\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < resSize; i++) {\n        free(res[i]);\n    }\n    free(res);\n    free(nums);\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(308, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> nums(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> nums[i];\n    }\n    sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());\n    vector<vector<int>> res;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n        if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;\n        int left = i + 1, right = n - 1;\n        while (left < right) {\n            int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];\n            if (sum == 0) {\n                res.push_back({nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]});\n                while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left + 1]) left++;\n                while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right - 1]) right--;\n                left++;\n                right--;\n            } else if (sum < 0) {\n                left++;\n            } else {\n                right--;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << \"[\";\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)res.size(); i++) {\n        cout << \"[\" << res[i][0] << \",\" << res[i][1] << \",\" << res[i][2] << \"]\";\n        if (i != (int)res.size() - 1) cout << \",\";\n    }\n    cout << \"]\" << endl;\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(308, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] nums = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            nums[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n        Arrays.sort(nums);\n        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;\n            int left = i + 1, right = n - 1;\n            while (left < right) {\n                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];\n                if (sum == 0) {\n                    res.add(Arrays.asList(nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]));\n                    while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left + 1]) left++;\n                    while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right - 1]) right--;\n                    left++;\n                    right--;\n                } else if (sum < 0) {\n                    left++;\n                } else {\n                    right--;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        sb.append(\"[\");\n        for (int i = 0; i < res.size(); i++) {\n            sb.append(\"[\");\n            sb.append(res.get(i).get(0)).append(\",\");\n            sb.append(res.get(i).get(1)).append(\",\");\n            sb.append(res.get(i).get(2));\n            sb.append(\"]\");\n            if (i != res.size() - 1) sb.append(\",\");\n        }\n        sb.append(\"]\");\n        System.out.println(sb.toString());\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(308, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nlet lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    lines.push(line.trim());\n});\n\nrl.on(\'close\', () => {\n    const n = parseInt(lines[0]);\n    const nums = lines[1].split(\' \').map(Number);\n    nums.sort((a, b) => a - b);\n    const res = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n        if (i > 0 && nums[i] === nums[i - 1]) continue;\n        let left = i + 1, right = n - 1;\n        while (left < right) {\n            const sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];\n            if (sum === 0) {\n                res.push([nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]]);\n                while (left < right && nums[left] === nums[left + 1]) left++;\n                while (left < right && nums[right] === nums[right - 1]) right--;\n                left++;\n                right--;\n            } else if (sum < 0) {\n                left++;\n            } else {\n                right--;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    let sb = \'[\';\n    for (let i = 0; i < res.length; i++) {\n        sb += \'[\';\n        sb += res[i][0] + \',\';\n        sb += res[i][1] + \',\';\n        sb += res[i][2];\n        sb += \']\';\n        if (i !== res.length - 1) sb += \',\';\n    }\n    sb += \']\';\n    console.log(sb);\n});', NULL, 1),
(308, 'PYTHON', 'n = int(input())\nnums = list(map(int, input().split()))\nnums.sort()\nres = []\nfor i in range(n - 2):\n    if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:\n        continue\n    left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n    while left < right:\n        s = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right]\n        if s == 0:\n            res.append([nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]])\n            while left < right and nums[left] == nums[left + 1]:\n                left += 1\n            while left < right and nums[right] == nums[right - 1]:\n                right -= 1\n            left += 1\n            right -= 1\n        elif s < 0:\n            left += 1\n        else:\n            right -= 1\nsb = \"[\"\nfor i in range(len(res)):\n    sb += \"[\" + \",\".join(map(str, res[i])) + \"]\"\n    if i != len(res) - 1:\n        sb += \",\"\nsb += \"]\"\nprint(sb)', NULL, 1),
(309, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    struct ListNode *next;\n} ListNode;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) != 1) return 0;\n\n    int *vals = (int *)malloc(sizeof(int) * (n > 0 ? n : 1));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &vals[i]);\n    }\n\n    int pos;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &pos);\n\n    if (n == 0) {\n        printf(\"false\\n\");\n        free(vals);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    ListNode **nodes = (ListNode **)malloc(sizeof(ListNode *) * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        nodes[i] = (ListNode *)malloc(sizeof(ListNode));\n        nodes[i]->val = vals[i];\n        nodes[i]->next = NULL;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n        nodes[i]->next = nodes[i + 1];\n    }\n\n    if (pos != -1) {\n        nodes[n - 1]->next = nodes[pos];\n    }\n\n    ListNode *slow = nodes[0];\n    ListNode *fast = nodes[0];\n    int hasCycle = 0;\n\n    while (fast != NULL && fast->next != NULL) {\n        slow = slow->next;\n        fast = fast->next->next;\n        if (slow == fast) {\n            hasCycle = 1;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%s\\n\", hasCycle ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        free(nodes[i]);\n    }\n    free(nodes);\n    free(vals);\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(309, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val;\n    ListNode* next;\n    ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> vals(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> vals[i];\n    }\n    int pos;\n    cin >> pos;\n\n    if (n == 0) {\n        cout << \"false\" << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    vector<ListNode*> nodes(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        nodes[i] = new ListNode(vals[i]);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n        nodes[i]->next = nodes[i + 1];\n    }\n    if (pos != -1) {\n        nodes[n - 1]->next = nodes[pos];\n    }\n\n    ListNode* slow = nodes[0];\n    ListNode* fast = nodes[0];\n    bool hasCycle = false;\n    while (fast != nullptr && fast->next != nullptr) {\n        slow = slow->next;\n        fast = fast->next->next;\n        if (slow == fast) {\n            hasCycle = true;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << (hasCycle ? \"true\" : \"false\") << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(309, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class ListNode {\n        int val;\n        ListNode next;\n        ListNode(int x) { val = x; }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] vals = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            vals[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n        int pos = sc.nextInt();\n\n        if (n == 0) {\n            System.out.println(\"false\");\n            return;\n        }\n\n        ListNode[] nodes = new ListNode[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            nodes[i] = new ListNode(vals[i]);\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n            nodes[i].next = nodes[i + 1];\n        }\n        if (pos != -1) {\n            nodes[n - 1].next = nodes[pos];\n        }\n\n        ListNode slow = nodes[0];\n        ListNode fast = nodes[0];\n        boolean hasCycle = false;\n        while (fast != null && fast.next != null) {\n            slow = slow.next;\n            fast = fast.next.next;\n            if (slow == fast) {\n                hasCycle = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(hasCycle ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(309, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nlet lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    lines.push(line.trim());\n});\n\nrl.on(\'close\', () => {\n    const n = parseInt(lines[0]);\n    const vals = lines[1] ? lines[1].split(\' \').map(Number) : [];\n    const pos = parseInt(lines[2]);\n\n    if (n === 0) {\n        console.log(\"false\");\n        return;\n    }\n\n    class ListNode {\n        constructor(x) {\n            this.val = x;\n            this.next = null;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const nodes = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        nodes.push(new ListNode(vals[i]));\n    }\n    for (let i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n        nodes[i].next = nodes[i + 1];\n    }\n    if (pos !== -1) {\n        nodes[n - 1].next = nodes[pos];\n    }\n\n    let slow = nodes[0];\n    let fast = nodes[0];\n    let hasCycle = false;\n    while (fast !== null && fast.next !== null) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n        if (slow === fast) {\n            hasCycle = true;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    console.log(hasCycle ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n});', NULL, 1),
(309, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    vals = list(map(int, data[1:1+n]))\n    pos = int(data[1+n])\n\n    if n == 0:\n        print(\"false\")\n        return\n\n    class ListNode:\n        __slots__ = (\'val\', \'next\')\n        def __init__(self, x):\n            self.val = x\n            self.next = None\n\n    nodes = [ListNode(v) for v in vals]\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        nodes[i].next = nodes[i + 1]\n    if pos != -1:\n        nodes[n - 1].next = nodes[pos]\n\n    slow = nodes[0]\n    fast = nodes[0]\n    has_cycle = False\n    while fast is not None and fast.next is not None:\n        slow = slow.next\n        fast = fast.next.next\n        if slow is fast:\n            has_cycle = True\n            break\n\n    print(\"true\" if has_cycle else \"false\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(310, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nvoid swap(int *a, int *b) {\n    int t = *a;\n    *a = *b;\n    *b = t;\n}\n\nvoid heapify(int *heap, int size, int i) {\n    int smallest = i;\n    int left = 2 * i + 1;\n    int right = 2 * i + 2;\n\n    if (left < size && heap[left] < heap[smallest]) {\n        smallest = left;\n    }\n    if (right < size && heap[right] < heap[smallest]) {\n        smallest = right;\n    }\n    if (smallest != i) {\n        swap(&heap[i], &heap[smallest]);\n        heapify(heap, size, smallest);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid push(int *heap, int *size, int value) {\n    heap[*size] = value;\n    (*size)++;\n    int i = *size - 1;\n    while (i > 0) {\n        int parent = (i - 1) / 2;\n        if (heap[parent] <= heap[i]) {\n            break;\n        }\n        swap(&heap[parent], &heap[i]);\n        i = parent;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid pop(int *heap, int *size) {\n    heap[0] = heap[*size - 1];\n    (*size)--;\n    heapify(heap, *size, 0);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &k);\n\n    int *heap = (int *)malloc(sizeof(int) * (k + 1));\n    int size = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int x;\n        scanf(\"%d\", &x);\n        push(heap, &size, x);\n        if (size > k) {\n            pop(heap, &size);\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", heap[0]);\n\n    free(heap);\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(310, 'CPP', '#include <iostream>\n#include <queue>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int x;\n        cin >> x;\n        pq.push(x);\n        if ((int)pq.size() > k) {\n            pq.pop();\n        }\n    }\n    cout << pq.top() << endl;\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
(310, 'JAVA', 'import java.util.PriorityQueue;\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int x = sc.nextInt();\n            pq.offer(x);\n            if (pq.size() > k) {\n                pq.poll();\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(pq.peek());\n    }\n}', NULL, 1),
(310, 'JAVASCRIPT', 'const readline = require(\'readline\');\n\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\n\nlet lines = [];\nrl.on(\'line\', (line) => {\n    lines.push(line.trim());\n    if (lines.length === 2) {\n        const [n, k] = lines[0].split(\' \').map(Number);\n        const nums = lines[1].split(\' \').map(Number);\n        const pq = [];\n        const push = (x) => {\n            pq.push(x);\n            let i = pq.length - 1;\n            while (i > 0) {\n                const p = (i - 1) >> 1;\n                if (pq[p] <= pq[i]) break;\n                [pq[p], pq[i]] = [pq[i], pq[p]];\n                i = p;\n            }\n        };\n        const pop = () => {\n            const top = pq[0];\n            const last = pq.pop();\n            if (pq.length > 0) {\n                pq[0] = last;\n                let i = 0;\n                while (true) {\n                    let l = i * 2 + 1, r = i * 2 + 2, m = i;\n                    if (l < pq.length && pq[l] < pq[m]) m = l;\n                    if (r < pq.length && pq[r] < pq[m]) m = r;\n                    if (m === i) break;\n                    [pq[i], pq[m]] = [pq[m], pq[i]];\n                    i = m;\n                }\n            }\n            return top;\n        };\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            push(nums[i]);\n            if (pq.length > k) pop();\n        }\n        console.log(pq[0]);\n        rl.close();\n    }\n});', NULL, 1),
(310, 'PYTHON', 'import sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    nums = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    heap = []\n    for x in nums:\n        heapq.heappush(heap, x)\n        if len(heap) > k:\n            heapq.heappop(heap)\n    print(heap[0])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()', NULL, 1),
(311, 'C', '#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int nums[n];\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &nums[i]);\n    }\n    int left = 0, right = n - 1;\n    while (left < right) {\n        int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;\n        if (nums[mid] > nums[mid + 1]) {\n            right = mid;\n        } else {\n            left = mid + 1;\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", left);\n    return 0;\n}', NULL, 1),
